        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The change is submitted. Summary of what was done:\n\n**Change:** In `src/itsdangerous/signer.py`, `_make_keys_list` now raises `ValueError(\"The iterable of secret keys must not be empty.\")` when a non-str/bytes `secret_key` iterable produces no keys.\n\n**Why this covers the requirements:**\n- **Empty lists/tuples/one-shot iterators rejected immediately** — the list comprehension fully consumes the iterable before the emptiness check, so even a generator that yields nothing triggers the error at `Signer(...)` construction time, not later at signing/key access.\n- **Individual string and bytes keys preserved** — the `isinstance(secret_key, (str, bytes))` branch returns early and is untouched, so `\"\"` and `b\"\"` still become `[b\"\"]`.\n- **Nonempty collections preserved** — the comprehension and return path are identical to before for any nonempty iterable, so signing, verification, tamper rejection, and oldest-to-newest key rotation are unaffected.\n\nNo tests were run locally (no execution environment); correctness was verified by code inspection.",
